c.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/climate-quiz-image-768x474.png 768w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/climate-quiz-image-1536x948.png 1536w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/climate-quiz-image-324x200.png 324w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/climate-quiz-image-200x123.png 200w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/climate-quiz-image.png 1750w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 1024px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 1024\/632;\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-column stk-block-column stk-column stk-block stk-beda32d stk-block-background\" data-v=\"4\" data-block-id=\"beda32d\"><style>.stk-beda32d-inner-blocks{align-items:center !important;justify-content:center !important}.stk-beda32d{background-color:#ed7303 !important;padding-top:30px !important;padding-right:50px !important;padding-bottom:30px !important;padding-left:50px !important}.stk-beda32d:before{background-color:#ed7303 !important}<\/style><div class=\"stk-column-wrapper stk-block-column__content stk-container stk-beda32d-container stk--no-background stk--no-padding\"><div class=\"stk--column-flex stk-block-content stk-inner-blocks stk-beda32d-inner-blocks\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color\">What are the four main spheres of the Earth\u2019s system?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">A. Atmosphere, geosphere, biosphere, hydrosphere<br>B. Ecosphere, lithosphere, hydrosphere, atmosphere<br>C. Geosphere, stratosphere, biosphere, magnetosphere<br>D. Troposphere, cryosphere, mesosphere, plasmasphere<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n<\/div><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-column stk-block-column stk-column stk-block stk-1f5a74c stk-block-background\" data-v=\"4\" data-block-id=\"1f5a74c\"><style>.stk-1f5a74c-inner-blocks{align-items:center !important;justify-content:center !important}.stk-1f5a74c{background-color:#00b0cc !important;padding-top:30px !important;padding-right:100px !important;padding-bottom:30px !important;padding-left:100px !important}.stk-1f5a74c:before{background-color:#00b0cc !important}@media screen and (max-width:767px){.stk-1f5a74c{padding-top:30px !important;padding-right:50px !important;padding-bottom:30px !important;padding-left:50px !important}}<\/style><div class=\"stk-column-wrapper stk-block-column__content stk-container stk-1f5a74c-container stk--no-background stk--no-padding\"><div class=\"stk--column-flex stk-block-content stk-inner-blocks stk-1f5a74c-inner-blocks\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color\">A. Atmosphere, geosphere, biosphere, hydrosphere<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">Geographers break down the Earth\u2019s system into four major subsystems called spheres that make up the world\u2019s air (atmosphere), water (hydrosphere), land (geosphere), and living organisms (biosphere).<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">Frozen water (glaciers, ice, hail, snow) is also known as the cryosphere.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https:\/\/www.soas.ac.uk\/cedep-demos\/000_P500_ESM_K3736-Demo\/unit1\/page_15.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Find out more<\/a><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-column stk-block-column stk-column stk-block stk-c1858c6 stk-block-background\" data-v=\"4\" data-block-id=\"c1858c6\"><style>.stk-c1858c6-inner-blocks{align-items:center !important;justify-content:center !important}.stk-c1858c6{background-color:#ed7303 !important;padding-top:30px !important;padding-right:50px !important;padding-bottom:30px !important;padding-left:50px !important}.stk-c1858c6:before{background-color:#ed7303 !important}<\/style><div class=\"stk-column-wrapper stk-block-column__content stk-container stk-c1858c6-container stk--no-background stk--no-padding\"><div class=\"stk--column-flex stk-block-content stk-inner-blocks stk-c1858c6-inner-blocks\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color\">Which of these is NOT weather?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-text-color has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">A. Ocean surface temperatures<br>B. Today\u2019s rainfall<br>C. This week\u2019s wind direction<br>D. Yesterday\u2019s humidity<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n<\/div><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-column stk-block-column stk-column stk-block stk-ab1250e stk-block-background\" data-v=\"4\" data-block-id=\"ab1250e\"><style>.stk-ab1250e-inner-blocks{align-items:center !important;justify-content:center !important}.stk-ab1250e{background-color:#00b0cc !important;padding-top:30px !important;padding-right:100px !important;padding-bottom:30px !important;padding-left:100px !important}.stk-ab1250e:before{background-color:#00b0cc !important}@media screen and (max-width:767px){.stk-ab1250e{padding-top:30px !important;padding-right:50px !important;padding-bottom:30px !important;padding-left:50px !important}}<\/style><div class=\"stk-column-wrapper stk-block-column__content stk-container stk-ab1250e-container stk--no-background stk--no-padding\"><div class=\"stk--column-flex stk-block-content stk-inner-blocks stk-ab1250e-inner-blocks\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color\">A. Ocean surface temperature<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">Weather refers to hourly, daily or weekly meteorological events. Climate change, like ocean surface temperature, refers to long-term change.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https:\/\/education.nationalgeographic.org\/resource\/weather-or-climate-whats-difference\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Find out more<\/a><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-column stk-block-column stk-column stk-block stk-6ab5105 stk-block-background\" data-v=\"4\" data-block-id=\"6ab5105\"><style>.stk-6ab5105-inner-blocks{align-items:center !important;justify-content:center !important}.stk-6ab5105{background-color:#ed7303 !important;padding-top:30px !important;padding-right:50px !important;padding-bottom:30px !important;padding-left:50px !important}.stk-6ab5105:before{background-color:#ed7303 !important}<\/style><div class=\"stk-column-wrapper stk-block-column__content stk-container stk-6ab5105-container stk--no-background stk--no-padding\"><div class=\"stk--column-flex stk-block-content stk-inner-blocks stk-6ab5105-inner-blocks\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color\">Carbon dioxide is made up of which elements?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-text-color has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">A. Carbon, methane and oxygen<br>B. Carbon and oxygen<br>C. Oxygen and water vapour<br>D. Carbon monoxide and methane<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n<\/div><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-column stk-block-column stk-column stk-block stk-17bc48f stk-block-background\" data-v=\"4\" data-block-id=\"17bc48f\"><style>.stk-17bc48f-inner-blocks{align-items:center !important;justify-content:center !important}.stk-17bc48f{background-color:#00b0cc !important;padding-top:30px !important;padding-right:100px !important;padding-bottom:30px !important;padding-left:100px !important}.stk-17bc48f:before{background-color:#00b0cc !important}@media screen and (max-width:767px){.stk-17bc48f{padding-top:30px !important;padding-right:50px !important;padding-bottom:30px !important;padding-left:50px !important}}<\/style><div class=\"stk-column-wrapper stk-block-column__content stk-container stk-17bc48f-container stk--no-background stk--no-padding\"><div class=\"stk--column-flex stk-block-content stk-inner-blocks stk-17bc48f-inner-blocks\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color\">B. Carbon and Oxygen<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">Carbon dioxide is a chemical compound composed of a carbon atom and two oxygen atoms. Carbon dioxide is a greenhouse gas. The over production of greenhouse gasses creates a cover that traps the sun\u2019s heat energy around earth, warming our planet and its oceans.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https:\/\/www.bbc.co.uk\/bitesize\/topics\/z3fv4wx\/articles\/zndkxyc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Find out more<\/a><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-column stk-block-column stk-column stk-block stk-28d7fa3 stk-block-background\" data-v=\"4\" data-block-id=\"28d7fa3\"><style>.stk-28d7fa3-inner-blocks{align-items:center !important;justify-content:center !important}.stk-28d7fa3{background-color:#ed7303 !important;padding-top:30px !important;padding-right:50px !important;padding-bottom:30px !important;padding-left:50px !important}.stk-28d7fa3:before{background-color:#ed7303 !important}<\/style><div class=\"stk-column-wrapper stk-block-column__content stk-container stk-28d7fa3-container stk--no-background stk--no-padding\"><div class=\"stk--column-flex stk-block-content stk-inner-blocks stk-28d7fa3-inner-blocks\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color\">Which of these is NOT a greenhouse gas?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-text-color has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">A. Ozone<br>B. Nitrous oxide (N2O)<br>C. Methane (CH4)<br>D. Oxygen (O)<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n<\/div><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-column stk-block-column stk-column stk-block stk-c97cc59 stk-block-background\" data-v=\"4\" data-block-id=\"c97cc59\"><style>.stk-c97cc59-inner-blocks{align-items:center !important;justify-content:center !important}.stk-c97cc59{background-color:#00b0cc !important;padding-top:30px !important;padding-right:100px !important;padding-bottom:30px !important;padding-left:100px !important}.stk-c97cc59:before{background-color:#00b0cc !important}@media screen and (max-width:767px){.stk-c97cc59{padding-top:30px !important;padding-right:50px !important;padding-bottom:30px !important;padding-left:50px !important}}<\/style><div class=\"stk-column-wrapper stk-block-column__content stk-container stk-c97cc59-container stk--no-background stk--no-padding\"><div class=\"stk--column-flex stk-block-content stk-inner-blocks stk-c97cc59-inner-blocks\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color\">D. Oxygen (O)<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">Oxygen on its own is not considered to be a greenhouse gas because it does not have the molecular structure needed to trap infrared radiation. The main greenhouse gases are carbon dioxide, methane, water vapour, ozone, nitrous oxide, and CFCs (Chlorofluorocarbons).<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https:\/\/www.bgs.ac.uk\/discovering-geology\/climate-change\/how-does-the-greenhouse-effect-work\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Find out more<\/a><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-column stk-block-column stk-column stk-block stk-10bc6aa stk-block-background\" data-v=\"4\" data-block-id=\"10bc6aa\"><style>.stk-10bc6aa-inner-blocks{align-items:center !important;justify-content:center !important}.stk-10bc6aa{background-color:#ed7303 !important;padding-top:30px !important;padding-right:50px !important;padding-bottom:30px !important;padding-left:50px !important}.stk-10bc6aa:before{background-color:#ed7303 !important}<\/style><div class=\"stk-column-wrapper stk-block-column__content stk-container stk-10bc6aa-container stk--no-background stk--no-padding\"><div class=\"stk--column-flex stk-block-content stk-inner-blocks stk-10bc6aa-inner-blocks\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color\">Carbon dioxide currently makes up how much of the earth\u2019s atmosphere?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-text-color has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">A. 0.04%<br>B. 40%<br>C. 4%<br>D. 8%<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n<\/div><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-column stk-block-column stk-column stk-block stk-b3a0a77 stk-block-background\" data-v=\"4\" data-block-id=\"b3a0a77\"><style>.stk-b3a0a77-inner-blocks{align-items:center !important;justify-content:center !important}.stk-b3a0a77{background-color:#00b0cc !important;padding-top:30px !important;padding-right:100px !important;padding-bottom:30px !important;padding-left:100px !important}.stk-b3a0a77:before{background-color:#00b0cc !important}@media screen and (max-width:767px){.stk-b3a0a77{padding-top:30px !important;padding-right:50px !important;padding-bottom:30px !important;padding-left:50px !important}}<\/style><div class=\"stk-column-wrapper stk-block-column__content stk-container stk-b3a0a77-container stk--no-background stk--no-padding\"><div class=\"stk--column-flex stk-block-content stk-inner-blocks stk-b3a0a77-inner-blocks\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color\">A. 0.04%<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">Carbon dioxide currently makes up around 0.04% of Earth\u2019s atmosphere. Even though this seems like a tiny amount, it is having a huge impact. Small changes in the Earth\u2019s heat balance can lead to large climatic changes.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https:\/\/climate.mit.edu\/ask-mit\/what-ideal-level-carbon-dioxide-atmosphere-human-life\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Find out more<\/a><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-column stk-block-column stk-column stk-block stk-c7678e3 stk-block-background\" data-v=\"4\" data-block-id=\"c7678e3\"><style>.stk-c7678e3-inner-blocks{align-items:center !important;justify-content:center !important}.stk-c7678e3{background-color:#ed7303 !important;padding-top:30px !important;padding-right:50px !important;padding-bottom:30px !important;padding-left:50px !important}.stk-c7678e3:before{background-color:#ed7303 !important}<\/style><div class=\"stk-column-wrapper stk-block-column__content stk-container stk-c7678e3-container stk--no-background stk--no-padding\"><div class=\"stk--column-flex stk-block-content stk-inner-blocks stk-c7678e3-inner-blocks\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color\">Which industrial sector is responsible for the most greenhouse gas emissions?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-text-color has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">A. Construction<br>B. Electricity and heat production<br>C. Transportation fuels<br>D. Agricultural production<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n<\/div><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-column stk-block-column stk-column stk-block stk-0ca7213 stk-block-background\" data-v=\"4\" data-block-id=\"0ca7213\"><style>.stk-0ca7213-inner-blocks{align-items:center !important;justify-content:center !important}.stk-0ca7213{background-color:#00b0cc !important;padding-top:30px !important;padding-right:100px !important;padding-bottom:30px !important;padding-left:100px !important}.stk-0ca7213:before{background-color:#00b0cc !important}@media screen and (max-width:767px){.stk-0ca7213{padding-top:30px !important;padding-right:50px !important;padding-bottom:30px !important;padding-left:50px !important}}<\/style><div class=\"stk-column-wrapper stk-block-column__content stk-container stk-0ca7213-container stk--no-background stk--no-padding\"><div class=\"stk--column-flex stk-block-content stk-inner-blocks stk-0ca7213-inner-blocks\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color\">B. Electricity and heat production<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">The burning of coal, natural gas, and oil for electricity and heat is the largest single source of global greenhouse gas emissions.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https:\/\/ourworldindata.org\/emissions-by-sector\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Find out more<\/a><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-column stk-block-column stk-column stk-block stk-2b534d4 stk-block-background\" data-v=\"4\" data-block-id=\"2b534d4\"><style>.stk-2b534d4-inner-blocks{align-items:center !important;justify-content:center !important}.stk-2b534d4{background-color:#ed7303 !important;padding-top:30px !important;padding-right:50px !important;padding-bottom:30px !important;padding-left:50px !important}.stk-2b534d4:before{background-color:#ed7303 !important}<\/style><div class=\"stk-column-wrapper stk-block-column__content stk-container stk-2b534d4-container stk--no-background stk--no-padding\"><div class=\"stk--column-flex stk-block-content stk-inner-blocks stk-2b534d4-inner-blocks\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color\">Which is the current epoch?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-text-color has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">A. Cenzozoic<br>B. Mezozoic<br>C. Holocene<br>D. Anthropocene<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n<\/div><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-column stk-block-column stk-column stk-block stk-43a536d stk-block-background\" data-v=\"4\" data-block-id=\"43a536d\"><style>.stk-43a536d-inner-blocks{align-items:center !important;justify-content:center !important}.stk-43a536d{background-color:#00b0cc !important;padding-top:30px !important;padding-right:100px !important;padding-bottom:30px !important;padding-left:100px !important}.stk-43a536d:before{background-color:#00b0cc !important}@media screen and (max-width:767px){.stk-43a536d{padding-top:30px !important;padding-right:50px !important;padding-bottom:30px !important;padding-left:50px !important}}<\/style><div class=\"stk-column-wrapper stk-block-column__content stk-container stk-43a536d-container stk--no-background stk--no-padding\"><div class=\"stk--column-flex stk-block-content stk-inner-blocks stk-43a536d-inner-blocks\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color\">C. Holocene &amp; D. Anthropocene<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">Epochs are units of time used to describe the geological timescale of earth. The official current epoch is called the Holocene, which began 11,700 years ago after the last major ice age. However, the Anthropocene Epoch is an unofficial unit of geologic time, which describes the most recent period in Earth\u2019s history when human activity started to have a significant impact on the planet\u2019s climate and ecosystems.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https:\/\/education.nationalgeographic.org\/resource\/anthropocene\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Find out more<\/a><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div><\/div>\n<\/div><div class=\"stk-block-carousel__buttons\"><button class=\"stk-block-carousel__button stk-block-carousel__button__prev\" aria-label=\"Previous slide\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" data-prefix=\"fas\" data-icon=\"chevron-left\" class=\"svg-inline--fa fa-chevron-left\" xmlns=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2000\/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 512\" width=\"32\" height=\"32\"><path fill=\"currentColor\" d=\"M34.52 239.03L228.87 44.69c9.37-9.37